  "question_1_modules": {
    "answer": "The pinned port does not explicitly enable modules. With CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD unset and no FMT_MODULE cache/option override, fmt 12.2.0 defaults FMT_MODULE to OFF. Merely using a modern compiler, or inspecting whether a -std=c++26 flag appears, does not decide this CMake variable branch.",
    "source_conditions": [
      {
        "fact": "The exact fmt port is 12.2.0#1. It passes FMT_CMAKE_DIR=share/fmt, FMT_TEST=OFF and FMT_DOC=OFF; neither FMT_MODULE nor CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD is supplied by this port.",
        "refs": [
          {
            "source": "ports/fmt/vcpkg.json",
            "path": "/Users/rmanaloto/.local/state/marketplace-tool-foundation/vcpkg-source-e4563094/source/ports/fmt/vcpkg.json",
            "sha256": "1a82f63057d79eb46c1c743079baed6aa36015acc54798cf6a86ba62bf3276db",
            "lines": [
              1,
              18
            ]
          },
          {
            "source": "ports/fmt/portfile.cmake",
            "path": "/Users/rmanaloto/.local/state/marketplace-tool-foundation/vcpkg-source-e4563094/source/ports/fmt/portfile.cmake",
            "sha256": "041c48f80df5d0a2ba4d1334d5887e723cfd231b0e18bf18d25480658e4b6231",
            "lines": [
              17,
              23
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "fact": "fmt starts FMT_USE_CMAKE_MODULES as FALSE. Automatic ON requires CMake >=3.28 AND CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD >=20. On the current relevant Ninja route, Ninja >=1.11 and GNU compiler >=15 or Clang >=16 are additional requirements. The code uses GNU >=15 despite its earlier comment saying GCC>=14. These checks determine the default of option(FMT_MODULE ...); an existing explicit FMT_MODULE cache value can override that default.",
        "refs": [
          {
            "source": "fmt/CMakeLists.txt",
            "path": "/Users/rmanaloto/.codex/worktrees/2a14/claude-code-marketplace/evidence/vcpkg-private/fmt-source/source/CMakeLists.txt",
            "sha256": "94acf4a02003fe017676806206a7946a3e92d5c44784cd9dd34aa224e7711e0a",
            "lines": [
              53,
              86
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "fact": "Only if FMT_MODULE is true does fmt add fmt-module and its alias. That target requests cxx_std_20. Native CMake module support uses a CXX_MODULES FILE_SET; the fallback GNU branch adds -fmodules-ts and the fallback Clang branch emits explicit compiler precompile commands. Those branches were read, not executed.",
        "refs": [
          {
            "source": "fmt/CMakeLists.txt",
            "path": "/Users/rmanaloto/.codex/worktrees/2a14/claude-code-marketplace/evidence/vcpkg-private/fmt-source/source/CMakeLists.txt",
            "sha256": "94acf4a02003fe017676806206a7946a3e92d5c44784cd9dd34aa224e7711e0a",
            "lines": [
              327,
              411
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "fact": "The vcpkg configure helper forwards linkage, C/C++ flags, the chainloaded toolchain, and additional VCPKG_CMAKE_CONFIGURE_OPTIONS and configuration-specific options; it does not itself assign CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD. -DFMT_MODULE=OFF can be supplied through the existing configure-option mechanism for an explicit source-level guard. A chainloader or additional configure option can change the default assumptions.",
        "refs": [
          {
            "source": "ports/vcpkg-cmake/vcpkg_cmake_configure.cmake",
            "path": "/Users/rmanaloto/.local/state/marketplace-tool-foundation/vcpkg-source-e4563094/source/ports/vcpkg-cmake/vcpkg_cmake_configure.cmake",
            "sha256": "7ebe11c78864d1a7917af7727186165fd0ac145f7f6c533d58c79321cb66ae39",
